# Vauxhall Zafira A seven-seat MPV, 1999-2005.
#
# The first Zafira: the compact seven-seater with the Flex7 seating that
# folded the third row into the floor, and the tall van-like body. UK sales
# from 28 May 1999.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Zafira
#
# Dimensions 4.317 x 1.742 x 1.684 m, wheelbase 2.694 m (Opel press release,
# 26 June 2024, cross-checked against the Wikipedia infobox).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the flank is
# traced from it.
#
# Colours: grade (a) for model year 2005, the Vauxhall Zafira 2005 Models
# Edition 2 brochure: Glacier White, Royal Blue and Flame Red solid; Star
# Silver, Silver Lightning and Moonland metallic; Ultra Blue, Digital Green
# and Black Sapphire pearlescent. The four modelled are named on it. For
# 1999-2004 no Vauxhall list was read. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
# Speed 195 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro May 1999; retires staggered 2009-2012 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-a.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-a.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-zafira-a/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the Holden-badged side reference is used for the shared
# shell only, with UK facelift trim and the exposed rear door handles that the
# UK photographs show. The Flex7 seating is not modelled behind the opaque
# glazing, and the hubcap inserts are flat decorative faces.


obj=citycar
